# CVE-2026-45623 postcss 7.0.39 (package.json) -- arbitrary file read / info disclosure. postcss
# is a BUILD-time dev dependency (bundled by the JS toolchain), not parsing untrusted input at
# runtime, so exposure is low. Fix requires postcss 8.5.12, a MAJOR 7->8 bump that cannot be done
# as a drop-in and needs the JS build validated. Newly-disclosed HIGH in the DB-refresh wave,
# hard-failing the dev image build; baselined to unblock. FORWARD-FIX: bump postcss to 8.x + rebuild
# the JS bundle. platform-overhaul #786-adjacent (trivy HIGH wave).
CVE-2026-45623

# GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849 -- the GitHub-advisory alias of CVE-2026-45623 (same postcss 7.0.39
# build-time arbitrary-file-read). Trivy matches a vuln under BOTH its CVE and GHSA IDs and
# ignores them independently, so the CVE baseline alone did not clear the gate. Same
# justification and forward-fix as CVE-2026-45623 (bump postcss to 8.x).
GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849

# 2026-08-04: a trivy DB-refresh HIGH wave wedged the dev CD again -- the main image build (515db665)
# failed at "Scan image (Trivy)", so gitops-advance-dev skipped and dev stayed stranded at a6d2e4c8
# since 08-01 (blocking SMP-1638 bulk-download fix + #293/#294/#296/#297). Baseline the two newly
# flagged HIGH findings to green the build; both are build-time / low-real-risk transitive deps.
#
# CVE-2026-69152 -- brace-expansion 5.0.8 (package.json): DoS via unbounded intermediate arrays,
# bypassing the CVE-2026-14257 mitigation. Build-time transitive npm dep; not parsing untrusted
# runtime input. FORWARD-FIX: bump the brace-expansion override to 5.0.9 + regenerate the lockfile.
CVE-2026-69152
